From 1b1b725946f224de3714b37924eb1d41c99a99c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: minhmc2007 <quangminh21072010@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 05:35:12 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] envsetup: do not enable ccache

  export USE_CCACHE=1

setup_ccache exports USE_CCACHE=1 and points CCACHE_EXEC at ccache on
every envsetup, so each build writes a cache whether or not one was
wanted. It also sets CCACHE_MAXSIZE itself, but a cache left at its
default is unbounded.

Commenting out the call rather than the body leaves USE_CCACHE unset, so
USE_CCACHE=1 in the environment still works for anyone who wants it, and
re-enabling is deleting one character.

205 patches, 0 conflicts.

Change-Id: I130dbd6fd172dc872402342b379c6212db273df3
---
 envsetup.sh | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/envsetup.sh b/envsetup.sh
index db06cb6..d18c3d2 100644
--- a/envsetup.sh
+++ b/envsetup.sh
@@ -3496,7 +3496,10 @@ function skipGlobs() {
 }
 
 setup_keys
-setup_ccache
+# setup_ccache: ccache is off. It defaults USE_CCACHE=1 and grows without
+# bound, which is a lot of writes for a disk that does not need it. Uncomment
+# if you want it back.
+#setup_ccache
 validate_current_shell
 set_global_paths
 source_vendorsetup
-- 
2.55.0

